Straight-line by design, so `BIT_GC=stress` cannot reach a safepoint here and
the collection count is legitimately zero. Codegen emits `bit_rt_safepoint` at
loop back-edges only (runtime/ABI.md §4) and this program has no loop: it
initialises one private scheduler block, one task block, spawns once, reads two
words and prints. There is nothing to root either — every block it touches is
untraced module state (§11.11), never a GC object — so a precise-rooting oracle
has no object here to be wrong about.

Adding a loop to earn the oracle would also destroy the property: the whole
assertion is that the live worker's `dqTail` did not move ACROSS THE SPAWN, and
a collection between the two samples could resume `main` on a different worker
and invalidate the comparison.
